<title>USA: INTERVIEW- Asahi/America backs estimates.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW- Asahi/America backs estimates.</headline>
<byline>Susan Spielberg</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asahi/America Inc, a distributor and maker of thermoplastic valves, piping systems and components, said on Monday it expects to report 1996 earnings in line with Wall Street estimates.</p>
<p>&quot;We are comfortable with the Street's estimates for sales and earnings,&quot; Leslie Lewis, chairman, president and chief exeuctive, said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Lewis cited an estimate of $0.77 a share for 1996, and said he sees sales of $38.5 million to $38.7 million for the year.</p>
<p>&quot;We look strong for the fourth quarter,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
